Word-list source for the v0.2.7 expansion

Repository: https://github.com/andifathulms/word-space
Revision: 6b2ce3432d5753d2b77724e0255ca6d4d019d34d
Files: data/answers.txt (2315 words), data/guesses.txt (12972 words)
Source statement: https://github.com/andifathulms/word-space/blob/6b2ce3432d5753d2b77724e0255ca6d4d019d34d/data/README.md

The source attributes these alphabetically sorted, five-letter English word
lists to Josh Wardle's original Wordle (2021), now owned by The New York Times
Company, via the cfreshman mirrors linked in its data README. It describes its
use as reproduction of a fact-like compilation for a noncommercial portfolio.
The repository provides no explicit open-source licence for these lists. This
notice records that statement; it does not relicense the data as MIT, Apache or
public domain, or claim affiliation with the original game or rights holders.

ZhBot uses only the word lists, preserving the answer/allowed-guess distinction
and merging them with its existing 3-10 letter collection. No game code,
branding or puzzle order was copied. Source hashes and the prior seed needed
for a non-overwriting database upgrade are in word_space_upgrade.json.
